Subject: [PATCH 62/62] PC5: the nested-task flag a program set no longer crashes it
 (Wine patch 0941)

Far Cry crashed as it started, in its CPU check (CrySystem.dll), with a
fault Wine reported as a read of FFFFFFFF: the check sets the
nested-task flag with popf, and the next return to the game faults
with it set (Wine bug 33275). Wine now clears the flag when such a
fault happens and runs the instruction again; Windows and Linux clear
it the same way. No other fault changes.
